        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "SHA-512 is the KDF step of the peer's ECDH exchange: the raw secp256k1 ECDH shared secret (serializepubkey of the negotiated pubkey) is hashed once with SHA-512, then SHA-256-hashed again at :426-427 to form the AES-256-CBC session key, and signed with hand-rolled ECDSA at :453. Changeable here (first-party code). Meets CNSA 2.0 digest size; the quantum weakness in this chain is the secp256k1 ECDH underneath, not the hash."
